  "id": "Compound::DB01045 - Gene::100861540",
  "verbalization": "Rifampicin is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p through multiple indirect pathways, primarily via its interaction with Cyp3a43. The evidence suggests that Rifampicin binds to Cyp3a43, which in turn is bound by Rifapentine, and Rifapentine subsequently binds to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p. This creates a chain of interactions where Rifampicin indirectly influences the expression or activity of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p through its effects on Cyp3a43. The lowest common ancestors in these paths indicate a shared relationship with antitubercular agents and N-Iminopiperazine, reinforcing the broader pharmacological context of Rifampicin’s action. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism by which Rifampicin may modulate the activity of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, likely through the regulation of Cyp3a43, which serves as a critical mediator in this interaction.",
